      "displayName": "César Pitti"
    },
    "starRating": "THREE",
    "comment": "Me pasó algo tragicómico.  Llené el tanque,  usamos los baños y quisimos comprar solamente medialunas para seguir viaje.  No nos las quisieron vender porque las reservaban para los que iban a desayunar ahí. Parece que el criterio es: no te venden porque se quedan sin para vender a posibles clientes. Digo posibles porque nadie asegura que  las vendieran.\nNo sería lógico que en plena temporada alta de turismo, reforzaran stock de todo?Cómo se entiende?\nIncreíble......\n\n(Translated by Google)\nSomething tragically funny happened to me. I filled up the tank, we used the restrooms, and we wanted to buy some croissants to continue our trip. They wouldn\u0027t sell them to us because they were reserving them for people who were going to have breakfast there. It seems their logic is: they won\u0027t sell to you because they\u0027ll run out to sell to potential customers. I say potential because there\u0027s no guarantee they would sell them. Wouldn\u0027t it make sense for them to replenish their stock of everything during peak tourist season? How does that make sense?\nUnbelievable...",
